class:: ChordStats
summary:: Duration-weighted statistics of chord states
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Tonal
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/HPCP, Classes/HarmonicPeaks

description::
Accumulates duration in 24 major/minor labels plus no-chord (default), or 108 extended labels plus no-chord, using the time between accepted observations. Returns distribution entropy, state-change rate and no-chord occupancy together with the most occupied chord. This is an original streaming summary of supplied classifications; it does not run another chord detector. Statistics cover the interval since creation or reset, rather than a fixed rolling window.



classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: root
Root index 0=C through 11=B, or -1 for no chord.

argument:: quality
Quality index from ChordTrack, or -1 for no chord. Out-of-vocabulary values count as no-chord.

argument:: trig
A positive value processes this control block. For FFT-derived features pass chain >= 0 so each analysis frame is used once; default 1 processes each control block.

argument:: reset
Positive values clear accumulated statistics. Use an impulse for a single reset.

argument:: vocabulary
Literal code::\triads:: or code::\extended::. Match the vocabulary passed to ChordTrack; this determines the number of states used to normalize entropy. Fixed at construction.

returns::
An Array: normalized 25-state or 109-state entropy, changes per second, no-chord duration fraction, dominant root, dominant quality.

examples::
ChordStats maintains streaming duration-weighted statistics of classified chords, returning normalized chord distribution entropy, state change rate (transitions/second), no-chord duration fraction, and dominant chord labels. In this example, chord transition rate modulates the depth of a stereo tremolo effect: static harmony produces a calm sustained sound, while rapid harmonic changes animate tremolo movement. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: displays real-time chord change rate.
code::
(
Routine({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("piano-chords.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic chords fallback
            Mix.ar(SinOsc.ar([261.63, 329.63, 392.00, 523.25] * LFNoise0.kr(0.5).range(1, 1.25))) * 0.15
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(2048), source, 0.25);
        var chroma = HPCP.kr(chain, size: 12, harmonics: 2, normalize: \max, fftSize: 2048);
        var chord = ChordTrack.kr(chroma, smooth: 0.05, trig: chain >= 0, vocabulary: \extended);
        var stats = ChordStats.kr(chord[0], chord[1], trig: chain >= 0, vocabulary: \extended);
        var chgRate = stats[1].lag(0.08);
        var tremolo = SinOsc.kr(4, 0, chgRate.linlin(0, 1.5, 0.0, 0.35).clip(0.0, 0.5), 1.0);
        var sound = source * tremolo * 0.25 ! 2;

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, chgRate.clip(0, 5)) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Chord Change Rate", ~mir2Bus, 0.0, 3.0, "chg/s");
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

